  "body": "PR #1671 certifies the selected k8 word's frame optimum at two exponents. This contribution audits its unchanged symbolic duals and proves that the same paid histogram minimizes the frame LP for **every `0 <= a <= 1/32`**. For **`0 < a <= 1/32`, every optimal assignment has exactly that histogram**, although its frames can differ. The interval includes the `1/99` planning target.\n\nThis is one scoped proof extension and arithmetic audit, **no new kappa or physical supplier**. Only `research/selected-k8-uniform-frame-audit/` is added. The source word, event/domain model, endpoints, scalar chronology, centre cut and cleanup/cone contract remain fixed. The original physical decoder construction gate is not claimed satisfied.\n\n### Exact evidence\n\n- Reconstructs all **23,004 LP columns, 17,507 rows and 135 component objectives**; a second column assembly works directly from the shared event graph and agrees on every cost and residual.\n- The 239 distinct rational residual vectors comprise one zero vector (16,564 columns), one exact square (10 columns), and 237 vectors (6,430 columns) proved positive uniformly by rational degree-eight Bernstein coefficients. No floating-point or solver output certifies the interval.\n- Strict positivity outside the identically-zero columns plus symbolic objective equality proves optimal-profile rigidity. Rank-one counts follow from the invariant local mass 5,586. A distinct feasible model assignment at gate G616 retains the full histogram.\n- Exact boundary controls show this particular dual fails for `min(r,2)` and at `a=1/20`. Neither control supplies a cheaper feasible assignment or contradicts #1671. The interval is not claimed maximal.\n\nThe written argument is in `PROOF.md`; `RESULT.json` retains every distinct residual/multiplicity and sign certificate. Canonical receipt: `859fcb8c40601ce3a1d453b5703f20268c5bfab2228aac8484e1cbba47aea703`.\n\n### Reproduce and validation\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/selected-k8-uniform-frame-audit\n```\n\nPassed on macOS 26.5.2 arm64 / CPython 3.12.12, standard library only:\n\n- Registered replay, metadata/source pins and **all eight test groups**, including integer-root arithmetic at three sample exponents, exact Bernstein basis identities, dual/objective/column/domain mutations, damaged sources/receipts, and optimized read-only relocation.\n- Optimized mathematical replay from a clean Git export of contribution commit **`cd696b3df479cd221ca812f2eb0804027a44da2f`** reproduces the same receipt.\n- `make selected-record-check` passes separately.\n- The pinned PR1671 package's separate checker was also replayed unchanged: `PASS_K8_FRAME_INDEPENDENT components=135 columns=23004 root_calibrations=72 graph_and_duality_match=True`.\n\nBoth new column assemblies **share the inherited event/domain model**; this is not an independent implementation or proof of the physical interface. Full selected cold replay, native/hosting admission, all-size/compiler, common-label/mutable-source, precision/tape, analytic/bit H1-H5 obligations, Lean and human review are unclaimed. Local checks do not establish hosted-CI success or maintainer acceptance.\n\n### Scope, pins and credit\n\n- Base: `418e40eb2572d930b58c1cf9b82b41c0fc7ee08d`.\n- Exact predecessor: #1671 at **`ce130d291f5ab6dd801544886a16f62d42d86118`**, rechecked open and unchanged. Its `DUALS.json.gz` is retained byte-for-byte with attribution and source pins.\n- Chooser nonce `4071338634dbc7c5d72c8e5f2a5a4633`, revision 3, `complex-rank-shape-decoder`; TASK.json declares the **changed** scope to an independent audit/extension after overlap found #1671.\n- [Coordination claim](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1659#discussioncomment-18916847). Final overlap at 06:45 UTC covered 407 open PRs including drafts, 332 Discussion records, and 710 local records; complete remote pagination and no warnings. This is metadata coverage, not a novelty guarantee. Current main `5e554ff58d01921747d27177045c0061f31e1ad1` preserves the selected record, instructions, catalogue and all three live inputs.\n- [Discussion #1674](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1674) changes helper endpoints and is complementary, outside this theorem. #1605 studies abstract reblocking/overhead rather than this fixed-word LP.\n\nCredit **Gareth Davidson / bitplane** for #1671's unchanged symbolic duals and selected-word theorem; **Aaron Wang / navinor** for the retained X4 frame model/method; and Jeremy Kothe, Rohan Arun, Hao Yan, icekylinx, DreamingOfClouds, eumemic, the earlier frame-method authors, Sagar Thakrar and Douglas Colkitt for the retained construction/coverage lineage. NOTICE.md and SOURCES.json preserve details.\n\nPrepared for **Ross Richardson with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance** in the mathematics, implementation, tests and writing. No subagents or independent human review. Apache-2.0. Selected evidence and predecessor files remain unchanged.\n\nThe concrete next step is one explicit scalar-dependency or gate-order change with a new dirty-state contract and complete cost screen. The old fixed-word certificate cannot certify that changed construction.\n",
